    <note type="translation" xml:lang="en">Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl al-Makkī al-Ḥulwānī. His father was a perfumer, and he (Ibrāhīm) was known as al-Ḥijāzī. He heard al-Musalsal and other works from al-Zayn al-Marāghī in 714 H. He died in Muḥarram 778 H.</note>
